/-
# Countable abelian verbal subgroups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 8.18)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.18 (Yu. G. Kleiman): is every countably
infinite abelian group a verbal subgroup of some finitely generated (soluble) relatively free group?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentClassFourVarietyLatticeKourovka3Problem53Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CountableAbelianVerbalSubgroupKourovka8Problem18Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.18 (Yu. G.
Kleiman). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700470 (`KOU-8.18`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A finitely generated relatively free group is `F_m / N` for a fully invariant subgroup `N` of the
free group `F_m` of finite rank (`IsFullyInvariant` of
Kourovka 3.53). The verbal subgroup `W(F)` of `F` defined by a set
`W` of words of `FreeGroup ℕ` is generated by all values of the words of `W` in `F`. The
parenthetical "(soluble)" is not formalized: Storozhev's paper was not readable, and the zbMATH
review of it (R. G. Burns, Zbl 0813.20028) states the question it answers as "Can every countable
abelian group occur as a verbal subgroup of some finitely generated relatively free group?",
answered with Ol'shanskii's technique (Geometry of Defining Relations in Groups); neither the review
nor any other source read says that the relatively free group can be taken soluble. The statement is
the unparenthesized question.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentClassFourVarietyLatticeKourovka3Problem53Wanted
  (IsFullyInvariant)

/-- The verbal subgroup `W(F)` of `F` defined by a set `W` of words: the subgroup generated by all
values of the words of `W` in `F`. -/
def verbalSubgroup (W : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) (F : Type*) [Group F] : Subgroup F :=
  Subgroup.closure {g | ∃ w ∈ W, ∃ f : FreeGroup ℕ →* F, f w = g}

/-- Kourovka 8.18 (Yu. G. Kleiman), without the parenthetical "(soluble)": every countably infinite
abelian group `A` is isomorphic to a verbal subgroup of a finitely generated relatively free group
`F_m / N` (`N` a fully invariant subgroup of the free group `F_m` of finite rank `m`). -/
def countableAbelianIsVerbalInRelativelyFree : Prop :=
  ∀ (A : Type) [CommGroup A] [Countable A] [Infinite A],
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (N : Subgroup (FreeGroup (Fin m))) (_ : N.Normal), IsFullyInvariant N ∧
      ∃ W : Set (FreeGroup ℕ), Nonempty (verbalSubgroup W (FreeGroup (Fin m) ⧸ N) ≃* A)

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 8.18 "Yes, it is", citing Storozhev, On abelian
subgroups of relatively free groups (1994); by the zbMATH review (R. G. Burns, Zbl 0813.20028),
Storozhev answers in the affirmative whether every countable abelian group occurs as a verbal
subgroup of some finitely generated relatively free group, using Ol'shanskii's technique. Source: E.
I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.18 (Yu. G. Kleiman);
resolution: A. Storozhev, On abelian subgroups of relatively free groups, Comm. Algebra 22 (1994),
2677-2701, Kourovka Archive, Problem 8.18: Yes, it is (Storozhev); main theorem as stated in the
zbMATH review Zbl 0813.20028 (R. G. Burns), https://doi.org/10.1080/00927879408824986.
-/
public theorem_wanted countableAbelianIsVerbalInRelativelyFree_holds :
    countableAbelianIsVerbalInRelativelyFree

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.CountableAbelianVerbalSubgroupKourovka8Problem18Wanted
